{
  "_comment": "Shared parity cases for the syntax highlighter. BOTH the author-time Python tool (tools/highlight_code.py, checked by tests/test_highlight_parity.py) and the runtime JS diff highlighter (cmhHighlightCode in assets/js/26-highlight.js, checked by tests/57-highlight-parity.spec.js) must classify each snippet the same way, so the two parallel implementations cannot drift (GH-REGRESS-HIGHLIGHT-PARITY). 'str'/'com'/'kw' list tokens that MUST land in that class; 'notStr' lists lone-quote tokens that must NOT be swallowed as a string (the PR #33 regression class: an UNTERMINATED single quote - a Rust lifetime or a YAML/Ruby apostrophe - must not run to end of line); 'notKw' lists runtime-side tokens that must not be wrapped in a keyword span. Known accepted divergence NOT asserted here: the runtime's compact tokenizer colors a C++ digit separator with PAIRED quotes (1'000'000 -> '000' as a string), which the Python tool avoids via a dedicated char-literal pattern; that is a minor cosmetic difference on a rarely-diffed construct, not the end-of-line over-match #33 fixed.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "lang": "rust",
      "code": "let data = local + val; let s: &'a str = \"hi\"; // note",
      "str": ["\"hi\""],
      "com": ["// note"],
      "kw": ["let"],
      "notKw": ["data", "local", "val"],
      "notStr": ["'a str = ", "'a"]
    },
    {
      "lang": "cpp",
      "code": "int r = foo(x); /* big */",
      "com": ["/* big */"]
    },
    {
      "lang": "yaml",
      "code": "name: don't # a note",
      "com": ["# a note"],
      "notStr": ["'t # a note", "don't"]
    },
    {
      "lang": "python",
      "code": "filter = local + process; x = 'hi' # done",
      "str": ["'hi'"],
      "com": ["# done"],
      "notKw": ["filter", "local", "process"]
    },
    {
      "lang": "javascript",
      "code": "const y = \"z\"; // trailing",
      "str": ["\"z\""],
      "com": ["// trailing"],
      "kw": ["const"]
    },
    {
      "lang": "css",
      "code": ".filter { content: local; animation: process; } /* c */",
      "com": ["/* c */"],
      "notKw": [".filter", "local", "process"]
    },
    {
      "lang": "sql",
      "code": "SELECT id FROM orders WHERE status = 'paid';",
      "str": ["'paid'"],
      "kw": ["FROM", "WHERE"]
    },
    {
      "lang": "batch",
      "code": "IF 1==1 ECHO Hello & REM a comment",
      "com": ["REM a comment"],
      "kw": ["IF"]
    },
    {
      "lang": "powershell",
      "code": "FUNCTION Get-Thing { RETURN $Name }",
      "kw": ["FUNCTION", "RETURN"]
    },
    {
      "lang": "html",
      "code": "<div class=\"cmh-note\" id=\"x\"> <!-- c --> hi</div>",
      "str": ["\"cmh-note\"", "\"x\""],
      "com": ["<!-- c -->"],
      "kw": ["div"],
      "notKw": ["class", "id"]
    },
    {
      "lang": "xml",
      "code": "<item name=\"a\"> <!-- x --> </item>",
      "str": ["\"a\""],
      "com": ["<!-- x -->"],
      "kw": ["item"],
      "notKw": ["name"]
    },
    {
      "lang": "json",
      "code": "{\"name\": \"cmh\", \"ok\": true, \"n\": 3}",
      "key": ["\"name\"", "\"ok\"", "\"n\""],
      "str": ["\"cmh\""],
      "kw": ["true"],
      "notStr": ["\"name\"", "\"ok\""],
      "notKey": ["\"cmh\""]
    },
    {
      "lang": "jsonc",
      "code": "{ /* blk */ \"a\": \"b: c\" } // note",
      "key": ["\"a\""],
      "str": ["\"b: c\""],
      "com": ["/* blk */", "// note"],
      "notKey": ["\"b: c\""]
    },
    {
      "lang": "json",
      "code": "{\"a\\\"b\": 1, \"c:d\": 2}",
      "key": ["\"a\\\"b\"", "\"c:d\""],
      "notStr": ["\"c:d\"", "\"a\\\"b\""]
    },
    {
      "lang": "json",
      "code": "{\"\": \"v\"}",
      "key": ["\"\""],
      "str": ["\"v\""],
      "notStr": ["\"\""],
      "notKey": ["\"v\""]
    },
    {
      "lang": "jsonc",
      "code": "{\"a\":1}/*c*/",
      "key": ["\"a\""],
      "com": ["/*c*/"],
      "notKey": ["/*c*/"]
    },
    {
      "lang": "jsonc",
      "code": "// \"notakey\": 1",
      "com": ["// \"notakey\": 1"],
      "notKey": ["\"notakey\""]
    },
    {
      "lang": "markdown",
      "code": "## Findings and next steps",
      "kw": ["## Findings and next steps"]
    },
    {
      "lang": "markdown",
      "code": "a **strong** and *soft* claim with `code` inline",
      "kw": ["**strong**"],
      "com": ["*soft*"],
      "str": ["`code`"],
      "notKw": ["claim", "inline"]
    },
    {
      "lang": "markdown",
      "code": "see [the spec](https://x.dev/a_b) <!-- note --> and <https://x.dev/p>",
      "str": ["https://x.dev/a_b", "<https://x.dev/p>"],
      "com": ["<!-- note -->"],
      "notKw": ["spec", "note"]
    },
    {
      "lang": "markdown",
      "code": "> quoted `code` with ~~old~~ text",
      "str": ["`code`"],
      "com": ["~~old~~"]
    },
    {
      "lang": "markdown",
      "code": "a **bold ** and *soft * stay plain",
      "notKw": ["**bold **", "bold"],
      "notStr": ["*soft *"]
    },
    {
      "lang": "markdown",
      "code": "> > deeply quoted with ```a``b``` inline",
      "str": ["```a``b```"]
    },
    {
      "lang": "md",
      "code": "# Title with `md` alias",
      "kw": ["# Title with `md` alias"],
      "notStr": ["`md`"]
    }
  ]
}
